-- title:
--   Theorem 3.21 — pure coloured graphons: cut-norm topology, $\cong$ iff $\delta_\square=0$, convergence iff $\delta_\square\to0$
-- statement:
--   Let $\kappa\ge1$ and consider coloured graphons on $[0,1]$ with Lebesgue measure, with the coloured cut norm (3.72) and the coloured cut distance $\delta_\square$ (3.73).
--
--   1. On the set $\mathcal W_{\mathrm{pure}}$ of pure coloured graphons, the metric topology of the cut norm (3.72) coincides with the restriction of the product topology of §2.4 (cut norm on the graphon, weak-* on the colouring).
--   2. For pure coloured graphons $W_1,W_2$,
--   $$
--   W_1\cong W_2\iff\delta_\square(W_1,W_2)=0 .
--   $$
--   3. For pure coloured graphons $W,W_1,W_2,\ldots$, as $n\to\infty$,
--   $$
--   W_n\to W\ \text{in }\widehat{\mathcal W}\iff\delta_\square(W_n,W)\to0 .
--   $$
--
--   So, for pure colourings, the coloured cut metric induces the topology of coloured graph limits, extending the classical uncoloured theory.
--
--   **Formalization Note** Clause 1 is an equality of the two topologies induced on the subtype of pure elements of `KGraphon volume κ`. $W_n\to W$ in $\widehat{\mathcal W}$ means $\tau(W_n)\to\tau(W)$ in $\mathbb R^L$. Measure-preserving bijections in (3.73) are bijective measure-preserving maps.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - encoding: the metric topology of (3.72) on W_pure and the restriction of the product topology → equality of TopologicalSpace.induced Subtype.val of colCutTop κ and of the KGraphon topology on {p // IsPureKGraphon p}; reason: the restriction of the topology generated by (3.72)-balls is the metric topology of the restricted metric
--   - encoding: measure-preserving bijections φ₁, φ₂ : [0, 1] → [0, 1] in (3.73) → Function.Bijective φ ∧ MeasurePreserving φ volume volume; reason: a Borel bijection of [0, 1] has a Borel inverse (Lusin–Souslin), which is then measure-preserving
--   - encoding: Wₙ → W in Ŵ → τ(Wₙ) → τ(W) in ℝ^L; reason: Definition 3.5 (W1) and Corollary 2.15
--   - encoding: [0, 1] with Lebesgue measure λ → unitInterval with volume and the Borel σ-field; reason: Remark 3.3: the Borel and Lebesgue σ-fields give the same results up to a.e. equality
--   - encoding: test graphs F ∈ U (unlabelled coloured graphs); limits as points of [0,1]^U → labelled coloured graphs on Fin (n+1) (LIdx κ); points of ℝ^L with the product topology; reason: t(F, ·) is invariant under relabelling (p.8), so equalities, convergence and limits over L and U agree; ℝ^L only changes the ambient space
--   - encoding: W₁ ≅ W₂ (Definition 2.6: one, and thus all, of the conditions of Lemma 2.5) → CEquiv: t(F, W₁) = t(F, W₂) for every coloured graph F; reason: condition (i) of Lemma 2.5, which Definition 2.6 lists as equivalent to the others
--   - encoding: colourings Ψ : Ω → Δκ, colours [κ]; pure colourings χ : Ω → [κ] → Ψ : Ω → Fin κ → ℝ with measurable nonnegative coordinates summing to 1 (IsKColouring); pure χ measurable with the point-mass colouring ofColour χ; reason: the same objects (Definition 2.1, p.7), with colours numbered 0, …, κ − 1
--   - encoding: κ ≥ 1 (Definition 2.1) → [NeZero κ]; reason: the same condition
-- source:
--   Janson, Lo, McDiarmid, Skeja, Skerman, Graphon Colourings and Limits of Graph Partitions, arXiv:2610.38599 (held version, sha256 3d198813a65d248922299a3380e10f238dbc5dcd3be060f7810b462bd5d3d10f), Theorem 3.21, p.29 (PDF p.29)

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_GraphonCheeger_Supplement_colCutDist

open MeasureTheory Filter Topology

namespace GraphonCheeger.Supplement

/-- Theorem 3.21, p.29 (Janson, Lo, McDiarmid, Skeja, Skerman, *Graphon Colourings and Limits of Graph Partitions*,
arXiv:2610.38599 (held version, sha256 3d198813…)): (i) on the set `W_pure` of all pure coloured graphons on `[0, 1]`, the
metric topology defined by the cut norm (3.72) coincides with the restriction to
`W_pure ⊂ W = W × Λ_κ` of the product topology of §2.4. (ii) For pure coloured graphons `W₁, W₂` on
`[0, 1]`, `W₁ ≅ W₂ ⇔ δ_□(W₁, W₂) = 0` (3.82). (iii) For pure coloured graphons `W, W₁, W₂, …` on
`[0, 1]`, `W_n → W` in `Ŵ` iff `δ_□(W_n, W) → 0` (3.83).

**Formalization Note.**
* Coloured graphons on `[0, 1]` (Lebesgue measure) are `KGraphon volume κ`; pure ones have
  colouring `ofColour χ` for a measurable `χ` (`IsPureKGraphon`). (i) is an equality of the two
  topologies induced on the subtype of pure coloured graphons: from `colCutTop` (the metric
  topology of (3.72)) and from the product topology (cut norm `×` weak-*).
* `δ_□` is the coloured cut distance (3.73) (`colCutDist`), and `W_n → W` in `Ŵ` means
  `τ(W_n) → τ(W)` in `ℝ^L` (Def. 3.5 (W1)). `κ ≥ 1` is `[NeZero κ]`. -/
theorem theorem_3_21 (κ : ℕ) [NeZero κ] :
    TopologicalSpace.induced
        (Subtype.val : {p : KGraphon (volume : Measure unitInterval) κ // IsPureKGraphon p} →
          KGraphon (volume : Measure unitInterval) κ) (colCutTop κ) =
      TopologicalSpace.induced
        (Subtype.val : {p : KGraphon (volume : Measure unitInterval) κ // IsPureKGraphon p} →
          KGraphon (volume : Measure unitInterval) κ) inferInstance ∧
    (∀ p q : KGraphon (volume : Measure unitInterval) κ, IsPureKGraphon p → IsPureKGraphon q →
      (CEquiv volume p.W p.Ψ volume q.W q.Ψ ↔ colCutDist p.W p.Ψ q.W q.Ψ = 0)) ∧
    (∀ (p : KGraphon (volume : Measure unitInterval) κ)
        (ps : ℕ → KGraphon (volume : Measure unitInterval) κ),
        IsPureKGraphon p → (∀ n, IsPureKGraphon (ps n)) →
        (Tendsto (fun n => tau volume (ps n).W (ps n).Ψ) atTop (𝓝 (tau volume p.W p.Ψ)) ↔
          Tendsto (fun n => colCutDist (ps n).W (ps n).Ψ p.W p.Ψ) atTop (𝓝 0))) := by sorry

end GraphonCheeger.Supplement
